Payee categorisation was tried with embeddings first. Measured against 164 payees, only 15% were confidently matched, and the tail was wrong in ways a person would never be — MAHALAKSHMI MESS came back as a hospital. Sending the same payees to an LLM with their payment pattern instead got every merchant right and inferred the personal-name shops from frequency and time of day. The first version missed transfers where money flows both ways, because only debits were sent; adding the credit side to the prompt fixed it.